# Consultation Window

This scope computes the deadline by which consultations must
begin after a request is made, and whether that deadline has
passed given a reference date.

Source pattern: Article 9 consultation clauses in EU trade
agreements.
Example: "consultations shall begin within one month from the
date of the request."
Example: "Should the consultations referred to in paragraph 1
fail to lead to agreement within 30 days of the Community's
request for consultations, the Community may utilise the right
to take action."

```catala
declaration scope ConsultationWindow:
  input request_date content date
  input consultation_window content duration
  input reference_date content date
  output consultation_deadline content date
  output deadline_passed content boolean
```

## Consultation deadline

The consultation must begin within consultation_window of the
request date.

```catala
scope ConsultationWindow:
  date round down
  definition consultation_deadline equals
    request_date + consultation_window
```

## Whether deadline has passed

Check whether the reference date is past the deadline.

```catala
scope ConsultationWindow:
  definition deadline_passed equals
    reference_date > consultation_deadline
```
